//@version=6
// =============================================================================
// Tradeify 50K Signals  (TradingView Pine Script v6 indicator)
// =============================================================================
//
// WHAT THIS IS
//   Signal prompts for trading NQ / MNQ by hand on a Tradeify 50K Sim Funded
//   account. On each confirmed bar it looks for the July NQ setups (Trend
//   Pullback, Opening Range Breakout, VWAP Reclaim, Failed Breakout Reversal,
//   VWAP Fade). When the best one passes the setup gates and the account
//   gates, it posts a LONG or SHORT prompt with a size that fits Tradeify's
//   limits and your own daily limits, a stop and two targets, and sends an
//   alert. It then follows the prompt as a virtual trade, posts its exits,
//   and uses the virtual P&L for the daily gates. It places no orders.
//
// THE RECORD, STATED PLAINLY
//   - In October, similar NQ setups (pullback, opening-range breakout, VWAP,
//     fades) failed on 14 years of real 1-minute NQ data after costs.
//   - On 49 regular sessions (Aug 24 - Oct 30, 2026, MNQ 5-minute; the July
//     Python engine run by trading/apex-50k/research/run_real.py at commit
//     5c4d89c, $100 risk, $300 daily stop, entries blocked from 15:50 ET)
//     these July setups took 18 trades, won 39% (7 of 18), and lost $12.58
//     per trade per micro: no better than seeded random entries (mean -0.12 R
//     against -0.08 R). This Pine port with its own defaults was not itself
//     replayed.
//   - So the signals are prompts, not advice, and not a proven edge. Past
//     results do not predict future results.
//   - Pine cannot see the account. The account inputs below must be typed
//     from the Tradeify dashboard every day for the sizes to be right. Until
//     they are, the table shows STALE: signals are still drawn, but in orange
//     and marked ACCOUNT FIGURES STALE, and their alerts carry that warning
//     (or are muted, per "When the account figures are stale").
//
// WHAT YOU SEE ON THE CHART
//   - LONG (teal) and SHORT (red) arrows with a label: size, entry, stop
//     (SL), target 1 and target 2, setup and score. Past signals are drawn
//     the same way, marked (past), so the chart shows where setups fired.
//   - Orange label: a live signal sized from stale account figures.
//   - Faded label with "no size": the setup fired but one contract risks
//     more than the budget (on NQ chart MNQ, or raise risk per trade).
//   - Grey arrow "setup held back": an account limit (floor, daily loss
//     limit, daily stop, profit lock, trade count, loss streak) blocked it.
//   - Blue / red / teal lines: entry, stop and targets of the open signal;
//     x marks and labels: its exits (T1, T2, stop, time, flat-by).
//   - Setups outside the entry window, near the flat-by, during warm-up or
//     while a signal is still open are not drawn.
//
// GETTING ALERTS ON A PHONE
//   1. Open MNQ1! (or the front MNQ contract) on a 5-minute chart and add
//      this indicator. Type today's figures from the Tradeify dashboard into
//      its settings. The table (top right) must not say STALE.
//   2. Install the TradingView app on the phone, log in to the same account
//      and allow its notifications.
//   3. On the chart: Alerts > Create alert. Condition: this indicator
//      ("Tradeify 50K Signals"), then "Any alert() function call". These
//      messages are sent once per bar close. Under Notifications tick
//      "Notify in app" so they reach the phone. Create it.
//      (Optional: the alertcondition alerts "Long signal", "Short signal",
//      "Exit" and "Flat-by in 10 minutes" carry short static messages; pick
//      "Once per bar close" for them.)
//   4. An alert keeps the inputs it was created with. After typing new daily
//      figures, delete the old alert and create a new one. An old alert goes
//      STALE at the first 18:00 ET session start after a 17:00 ET close that
//      is later than its as-of time. Its signals then carry the ACCOUNT
//      FIGURES STALE warning (or stop, if you chose "Draw only, no alerts").
//
// DAILY INPUTS (type them from the Tradeify dashboard before trading, flat)
//   Balance at last close, Trailing Max Drawdown floor (the dashboard
//   figure), highest end-of-day balance so far, today's realized P&L, trades
//   already taken today, and the date and time you read them ("as of"). The
//   figures are STALE when the as-of time is before the close of the
//   previous session (17:00 ET on the day the current session starts at
//   18:00 ET; Friday 17:00 ET for the Sunday session), so figures read
//   between sessions stay valid for the next one. Read between sessions,
//   today's realized P&L and trades taken are 0 (the balance at last close
//   already includes them). Type them while flat: a virtual trade or prompt
//   from before the as-of time is dropped when the live period starts.
//
// TRADEIFY 50K SIM FUNDED RULES MODELLED
//   From trading/tradeify-50k/rules.json, verified 2026-11-02. Re-check the
//   sources before relying on any number; the firm can change its rules.
//   - Trailing Max Drawdown 2,000, end-of-day trailing: floor = highest
//     end-of-day balance - 2,000, updated only at the end of each trading
//     day, never moves down; it locks at 50,100 once an end-of-day balance
//     reaches 52,100, or at once when a payout is requested. It is enforced
//     in real time on net liquidation (balance + open P&L); touching it fails
//     the account permanently. The indicator uses the higher of the floor you
//     type and the floor implied by the highest end-of-day balance.
//   - Contract cap: Growth and Lightning 4 minis or 40 micros (bought before
//     Sep 12, 2025: 5 or 50). Select Flex and Select Daily scale from the
//     highest end-of-day profit: under 1,500 -> 2 minis, 1,500 -> 3,
//     2,000 -> 4, kept once reached. Micros count 10 per mini; a micro is
//     detected from syminfo.root (MNQ, MES, MYM, M2K, MGC, MCL, ...).
//   - Daily loss limit (soft breach: trading pauses until the next 18:00 ET
//     session, the account stays open, losses can run past it): Growth and
//     Lightning 1,250, or 2,000 once the balance at last close is 53,000 or
//     more (legacy Growth: no limit from 53,000); Select Daily 1,000; Select
//     Flex none.
//   - Session 18:00-17:00 ET, flat by 16:45 ET (12:59 ET on early-close
//     days, which are not scheduled here: flatten those yourself).
//   - Consistency (Growth 35%, Lightning 20-30%, Select none) is a payout
//     rule. The daily profit lock input is a guard against one outsized day,
//     not the rule itself. Its Auto values fit the first payout only; after
//     a payout set it to Custom (see its tooltip).
//   - Not modelled: payouts, microscalping (more than 50% of trades and of
//     profit must come from trades held longer than 10 seconds), at least
//     1 trade per week, no hedging (also across correlated products and
//     accounts), algo rules. News trading is allowed.
//   Sources:
//     https://help.tradeify.co/en/articles/10495897-rules-trailing-max-drawdowns
//     https://help.tradeify.co/en/articles/10468321-rules-daily-loss-limit
//     https://help.tradeify.co/en/articles/12268167-essential-trading-rules-overview
//     https://help.tradeify.co/en/articles/11083796-growth-funded-account-payout-policy
//     https://help.tradeify.co/en/articles/12853966-select-flex-and-select-daily-payout-policies
//     https://help.tradeify.co/en/articles/10495938-lightning-funded-accounts
//     https://help.tradeify.co/en/articles/10495932-lightning-funded-account-payout-policy
//     https://help.tradeify.co/en/articles/10468320-rules-consistency-rule
//   Unverified (rules.json): whether the Growth consistency window resets per
//   payout cycle; whether the 2,000 DLL reverts if the balance falls below
//   53,000 (this indicator uses the balance at last close, the cautious
//   reading); the DLL is modelled on realized plus open P&L for the session;
//   Select scaling uses end-of-day profit (balance - 50,000).
//
// HOW A PROMPT IS SIZED
//   per-contract risk = (stop points + 2 ticks of modelled entry and stop
//            slippage) x point value + round-trip commission
//   budget = the smallest of: risk per trade; room to floor x max share;
//            DLL room - $100 (plans with a DLL); room to your own daily stop
//   qty    = floor(budget / per-contract risk), capped at the plan's limit
//   room to floor = balance at last close + today's realized P&L + virtual
//            P&L since the as-of time - floor
//   A setup that cannot be sized to 1 contract is drawn with a faded arrow
//   and a faded "no size" label with the reason and a hint, and sends no
//   alert. On NQ ($20/point) a $150 budget is below one contract's risk for
//   any 8-point stop ($171.50), so NQ setups are "no size": chart MNQ or
//   raise the risk. The table then shows PAUSED with the reason.
//
// HOW A SIGNAL IS GATED (the table shows ARMED, DRAW ONLY or PAUSED: reason)
//   Not drawn: the signal bar closes outside the entry window or within 20
//   minutes of flat-by, during warm-up, or while a virtual trade is open or
//   pending. Drawn grey as "held back", no alert: room to floor <= 0; the
//   DLL, your daily stop or the daily profit lock is hit; the day's trade
//   count or the losses-in-a-row limit is reached. Stale or future account
//   figures only add a warning: the signal is drawn orange and alerted with
//   ACCOUNT FIGURES STALE, or drawn with every alert muted if you chose
//   "Draw only, no alerts" (the table then says DRAW ONLY). With stale
//   figures the typed realized P&L and trades taken belong to an earlier
//   session: they stay in the balance but not in today's daily limits. Prompts are decided on confirmed bars only, so they do not
//   repaint within a session. Which bars are live depends on the current
//   time and the typed figures: after the session rolls, a reload or new
//   inputs, earlier bars are recomputed as past signals and can differ
//   from what was alerted. Keep your own record of the alerts you acted on.
//
// THE VIRTUAL TRADE (as the July Python backtest manages it)
//   Entered at the next bar's open + 1 tick (cancelled if that is past the
//   stop or target 1). Each bar: an open through the stop exits at the
//   open; a stop touch exits at the stop - 1 tick (a bar touching stop and
//   target counts the stop first); target 1 (the setup's T1: 1.5R, or less
//   for a VWAP Fade) takes half off and moves the stop to breakeven (a
//   single contract exits whole at T1); target 2 (the setup's T2) takes the
//   rest; flat-by exits at the close - 1 tick of the last bar that closes
//   5 minutes or more before the flat-by time (16:40 ET by default), so the
//   EXIT alert comes before the deadline; after 24 bars held it exits at
//   the close - 1 tick. Commission is charged per contract.
//
// LIMITS AND APPROXIMATIONS
//   - Virtual P&L assumes every prompt was taken and filled as modelled.
//     Real fills differ: keep typing your real realized P&L.
//   - The trade count is "trades already taken today" plus virtual trades
//     filled after the as-of time; the losses-in-a-row count and the virtual
//     P&L start at the as-of time. A review trade still open or pending at
//     the as-of time is dropped then, so the typed figures stand alone.
//   - Past sessions, and the current session before the as-of time, show
//     past signals at full colour, marked (past), gated with the typed
//     figures as a stand-in for that day's account. They never alert. Turn
//     them off under Display ("Show signals on past bars").
//   - The entry window is judged on the signal bar's close time; overnight
//     windows (start after end) are not supported.
//   - Setups, gates and indicators are copied from the compiled July port
//     (Apex 50K Eval Lab): EMA 9/21/50, Wilder ATR/RSI/ADX, session VWAP and
//     bands, ATR percentile, 3/3 pivots, prior-day high/low built on the
//     chart, 09:30-10:00 ET opening range, 15-minute bias from the last
//     completed 15-minute bar (request.security with lookahead on and [1]),
//     best candidate by score, then score >= 55, stop 8-60 points and net R
//     to target 1 >= 1.2 after costs. Built for a 1 to 5 minute chart.
// =============================================================================

indicator("Tradeify 50K Signals", shorttitle = "TradeifySignals", overlay = true,
     max_labels_count = 500, max_lines_count = 10)

// ------------------------------------------------------------ constants ----
TZ = "America/New_York"
int DAY_MS = 86400000
int WARMUP_BARS = 200
int SLIP_TICKS = 1

int REG_UP = 1
int REG_DOWN = 2
int REG_CHOP = 3
int REG_EXP = 4
int REG_QUIET = 5

// <<RULES:BEGIN>> Tradeify 50K Sim Funded, rules.json verifiedOn 2026-11-02
float START_BAL = 50000
float TMD = 2000
float TMD_LOCKED_FLOOR = 50100
float DLL_BASE = 1250
float DLL_RAISE_AT = 53000
float DLL_RAISED = 2000
float DLL_SELECT_DAILY = 1000
int MAX_MINIS = 4
int MAX_MINIS_LEGACY = 5
float SEL_T2_PROFIT = 1500
float SEL_T3_PROFIT = 2000
int SEL_T1_MINIS = 2
int SEL_T2_MINIS = 3
int SEL_T3_MINIS = 4
int MICROS_PER_MINI = 10
int FLAT_BY_CAP_MIN = 1005
int SESSION_START_H = 18
int SESSION_END_H = 17
// <<RULES:END>>

// Indicator rules (not Tradeify rules).
int TIME_STOP_BARS = 24
int FLATBY_NO_ENTRY_MIN = 20
int FLATBY_WARN_MIN = 10
int FLATBY_EXIT_MIN = 5
float DLL_MARGIN = 100
float LOCK_GROWTH = 1000
float LOCK_LIGHTNING = 600
int MAX_KEEP_LABELS = 490

PLAN_GROWTH = "Growth"
PLAN_FLEX = "Select Flex"
PLAN_DAILY = "Select Daily"
PLAN_LIGHT = "Lightning"
LOCK_AUTO = "Auto, first payout (Growth 1000, Lightning 600, Select off)"
LOCK_CUSTOM = "Custom"
LOCK_OFF = "Off"
COMM_AUTO = "Auto (1.50 per mini, 0.50 per micro)"
COMM_CUSTOM = "Custom"

// --------------------------------------------------------------- inputs ----
grpAcct = "Tradeify account (type from the dashboard every day)"
iPlan = input.string(PLAN_GROWTH, "Plan", options = [PLAN_GROWTH, PLAN_FLEX, PLAN_DAILY, PLAN_LIGHT], group = grpAcct)
iLegacy = input.bool(false, "Bought before Sep 12, 2025 (legacy limits)", group = grpAcct,
     tooltip = "Growth and Lightning only: 5 minis / 50 micros, and legacy Growth has no daily loss limit once the balance at last close is 53,000 or more.")
iBal = input.float(50000, "Balance at last close ($)", step = 50, group = grpAcct, confirm = true)
iFloor = input.float(48000, "Trailing Max Drawdown floor ($, dashboard figure)", step = 50, group = grpAcct,
     tooltip = "The floor shown on the Tradeify dashboard. If it is below the floor implied by the highest end-of-day balance, the higher one is used.")
iHiEod = input.float(50000, "Highest end-of-day balance so far ($)", step = 50, group = grpAcct,
     tooltip = "Sets the Select contract tier (from highest end-of-day profit) and checks the floor. The balance at last close is used if it is higher.")
iTodayPnl = input.float(0, "Today's realized P&L ($)", step = 10, group = grpAcct, confirm = true,
     tooltip = "Realized P&L of the current session (since 18:00 ET). Type 0 if you read the figures between sessions (17:00-18:00 ET or the weekend): the balance at last close already includes it.")
iTradesToday = input.int(0, "Trades already taken today", minval = 0, group = grpAcct, confirm = true,
     tooltip = "Trades taken in the current session (since 18:00 ET). Type 0 if you read the figures between sessions.")
iAsOf = input.time(timestamp("01 Jan 2026 00:00 -0500"), "Figures as of (date and time)", group = grpAcct,
     tooltip = "When you read the figures. STALE (signals still drawn and alerted with a warning, see Display) when this is before the previous session's 17:00 ET close (Friday's for the Sunday session). Virtual P&L is added from this time on. Type the figures while flat: a virtual trade from before this time is dropped.")

grpRisk = "Risk"
iRisk = input.float(150, "Risk per trade ($)", minval = 1, step = 10, group = grpRisk)
iShare = input.float(10, "Max share of room to floor per trade (%)", minval = 0.5, maxval = 100, step = 0.5, group = grpRisk)
iSelfStop = input.float(400, "Self-imposed daily loss stop ($, 0 = off)", minval = 0, step = 25, group = grpRisk)
iLockMode = input.string(LOCK_AUTO, "Daily profit lock (consistency guard)", options = [LOCK_AUTO, LOCK_CUSTOM, LOCK_OFF], group = grpRisk,
     tooltip = "No new prompts once the day's P&L reaches this, so one day does not dominate the profit for the consistency rule. Auto fits the first payout only (about 35% / 20% of 3,000). After a payout use Custom set to the consistency share of the profit needed for the next payout: Lightning 500 for payout 2 and 600 after (legacy Lightning 400); Growth 35% of (53,000 - balance after the last payout).")
iLockCustom = input.float(1000, "Custom daily profit lock ($)", minval = 1, step = 50, group = grpRisk)
iMaxTrades = input.int(3, "Max trades per day", minval = 1, group = grpRisk)
iMaxLosses = input.int(2, "Stop after N losses in a row", minval = 1, group = grpRisk)
iCommMode = input.string(COMM_AUTO, "Round-trip commission per contract", options = [COMM_AUTO, COMM_CUSTOM], group = grpRisk)
iCommCustom = input.float(1.50, "Custom round-trip commission per contract ($)", minval = 0, step = 0.1, group = grpRisk)

grpSess = "Session (America/New_York)"
iWindow = input.session("0935-1530", "Entry window (ET)", group = grpSess,
     tooltip = "A prompt is allowed when the signal bar closes inside this window.")
iFlatH = input.int(16, "Flat-by (hour : minute ET)", minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = grpSess, inline = "fb")
iFlatM = input.int(45, "", minval = 0, maxval = 59, group = grpSess, inline = "fb",
     tooltip = "Capped at 16:45 ET, Tradeify's flat-by time. No prompts within 20 minutes of it; a reminder alert 10 minutes before it; the virtual trade exits 5 minutes before it.")

grpSig = "Setups"
iUseTP = input.bool(true, "Trend Pullback", group = grpSig)
iUseORB = input.bool(true, "Opening Range Breakout", group = grpSig)
iUseVR = input.bool(true, "VWAP Reclaim", group = grpSig)
iUseFB = input.bool(true, "Failed Breakout Reversal", group = grpSig)
iUseFade = input.bool(true, "VWAP Fade", group = grpSig)
iMinScore = input.float(55.0, "Minimum setup score (0-100)", minval = 0, maxval = 100, step = 5, group = grpSig)
iMinStop = input.float(8.0, "Min stop (points)", minval = 0, step = 1, group = grpSig)
iMaxStop = input.float(60.0, "Max stop (points)", minval = 1, step = 5, group = grpSig)
iMinNetR = input.float(1.2, "Min net R to target 1 (after costs)", minval = 0, step = 0.1, group = grpSig)

grpDisp = "Display"
iLblSize = input.string("Small", "Label size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal"], group = grpDisp)
iShowReview = input.bool(true, "Show signals on past bars (no alerts)", group = grpDisp,
     tooltip = "Draws every past signal at full colour so the chart shows where the setups fired. Past signals never alert.")
iShowBlocked = input.bool(true, "Show setups blocked by an account limit (grey)", group = grpDisp,
     tooltip = "A setup that passed the setup rules but was held back by the drawdown floor, the daily loss limit, your daily stop, the profit lock, the trade count or the loss streak is drawn in grey with the reason. It never alerts.")
STALE_ALERT = "Draw and alert, with a warning"
STALE_QUIET = "Draw only, no alerts"
iStaleMode = input.string(STALE_ALERT, "When the account figures are stale", options = [STALE_ALERT, STALE_QUIET], group = grpDisp,
     tooltip = "Stale figures never hide a signal. With the first option the alert still goes out, marked ACCOUNT FIGURES STALE, and the size is worked out from the old figures: check the floor and the daily loss room on the Tradeify dashboard before entering.")
iShowTable = input.bool(true, "Show table", group = grpDisp)

// -------------------------------------------------------- symbol & costs ----
var array<string> MICRO_ROOTS = array.from("MNQ", "MES", "MYM", "M2K", "MGC", "MCL", "M6E", "M6A", "M6B", "MJY", "MSF", "MCD", "MBT", "MET", "SIL", "MHG", "MNG")
bool isMicro = array.includes(MICRO_ROOTS, syminfo.root)
float rtCost = iCommMode == COMM_AUTO ? (isMicro ? 0.50 : 1.50) : iCommCustom
float pv = syminfo.pointvalue
float tick = syminfo.mintick
float slipPx = SLIP_TICKS * tick
string lblSize = iLblSize == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : iLblSize == "Normal" ? size.normal : size.small

// ----------------------------------------------------- Tradeify account ----
bool isSelect = iPlan == PLAN_FLEX or iPlan == PLAN_DAILY
bool legacyOn = iLegacy and not isSelect
float hiEod = math.max(iHiEod, iBal)
float eodProfit = hiEod - START_BAL
int capMinis = isSelect ? (eodProfit >= SEL_T3_PROFIT ? SEL_T3_MINIS : eodProfit >= SEL_T2_PROFIT ? SEL_T2_MINIS : SEL_T1_MINIS) : legacyOn ? MAX_MINIS_LEGACY : MAX_MINIS
int capQty = capMinis * (isMicro ? MICROS_PER_MINI : 1)
float planDll = iPlan == PLAN_FLEX ? float(na) : iPlan == PLAN_DAILY ? DLL_SELECT_DAILY : iBal >= DLL_RAISE_AT ? (legacyOn and iPlan == PLAN_GROWTH ? float(na) : DLL_RAISED) : DLL_BASE
float floorRule = math.min(hiEod - TMD, TMD_LOCKED_FLOOR)
float floorUsed = math.max(iFloor, floorRule)
bool floorTypedLow = iFloor < floorRule - 0.5
float lockVal = iLockMode == LOCK_OFF ? float(na) : iLockMode == LOCK_CUSTOM ? iLockCustom : iPlan == PLAN_GROWTH ? LOCK_GROWTH : iPlan == PLAN_LIGHT ? LOCK_LIGHTNING : float(na)
string planName = iPlan + (legacyOn ? " (legacy)" : "")
string tagTxt = "Tradeify " + planName + " 50K"

// --------------------------------------------------------------- helpers ----
rNear(float p) =>
    na(p) ? na : math.round(p / syminfo.mintick) * syminfo.mintick
rDown(float p) =>
    na(p) ? na : math.floor(p / syminfo.mintick + 1e-9) * syminfo.mintick
rUp(float p) =>
    na(p) ? na : math.ceil(p / syminfo.mintick - 1e-9) * syminfo.mintick

etMinutes(int t) =>
    hour(t, TZ) * 60 + minute(t, TZ)

parseHM(string s, int at) =>
    float h = str.tonumber(str.substring(s, at, at + 2))
    float m = str.tonumber(str.substring(s, at + 2, at + 4))
    na(h) or na(m) ? na : h * 60 + m

fmtPx(float p) =>
    na(p) ? "-" : str.tostring(p, format.mintick)
fmtUsd0(float v) =>
    na(v) ? "none" : (v < 0 ? "-$" : "$") + str.tostring(math.abs(v), "#,##0")
fmtUsd2(float v) =>
    na(v) ? "none" : (v < 0 ? "-$" : "$") + str.tostring(math.abs(v), "#,##0.00")
fmtSigned(float v) =>
    na(v) ? "-" : (v < 0 ? "-$" : "+$") + str.tostring(math.abs(v), "#,##0.00")
addLine(string a, string b) =>
    a == "" ? b : a + "\n" + b

// ------------------------------------------------------------- clock -------
bool newDay = bar_index == 0 or time_tradingday != time_tradingday[1]
int etMin = etMinutes(time)
int closeMin = etMinutes(time_close)
float winStart = parseHM(iWindow, 0)
float winEnd = parseHM(iWindow, 5)
float tfMin = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period) / 60.0
int flatByMin = math.min(iFlatH * 60 + iFlatM, FLAT_BY_CAP_MIN)
string flatTxt = str.tostring(math.floor(flatByMin / 60), "00") + ":" + str.tostring(flatByMin % 60, "00")
// The virtual trade is closed at the close of the last bar that closes at
// least 5 minutes before the flat-by time (the first bar whose next close
// would be later), so its EXIT alert arrives before the deadline.
bool atFlatBy = closeMin + tfMin > flatByMin - FLATBY_EXIT_MIN and closeMin < 18 * 60
bool inWindow = not na(winStart) and not na(winEnd) and closeMin >= winStart and closeMin < winEnd and closeMin < flatByMin and not atFlatBy
bool nearFlatBy = closeMin < 18 * 60 and closeMin >= flatByMin - FLATBY_NO_ENTRY_MIN
bool fbWarnBar = closeMin < 18 * 60 and closeMin <= flatByMin and closeMin + tfMin > flatByMin - FLATBY_WARN_MIN
float minsSinceOpen = (time - timestamp(TZ, year(time, TZ), month(time, TZ), dayofmonth(time, TZ), 9, 30)) / 60000.0
bool sessDrive = etMin >= 570 and etMin < 600
bool sessMorning = etMin >= 600 and etMin < 690
bool sessLunch = etMin >= 690 and etMin < 810
bool sessPower = etMin >= 900 and etMin < 950

// Current session start: 18:00 ET of the previous day, or of today after
// 18:00 ET. The typed figures are STALE when their as-of time is before the
// previous session's 17:00 ET close (the same day as that start; Friday for
// a Sunday start or over the weekend): figures read after that close, with
// no trading since, are still valid.
// Bars from that start on are the current session; once a bar closes after
// the as-of time it is live (gated by the typed figures, alerts on).
int nowNoon = timestamp(TZ, year(timenow, TZ), month(timenow, TZ), dayofmonth(timenow, TZ), 12, 0)
int sessRef = hour(timenow, TZ) >= SESSION_START_H ? nowNoon : nowNoon - DAY_MS
int sessStartNow = timestamp(TZ, year(sessRef, TZ), month(sessRef, TZ), dayofmonth(sessRef, TZ), SESSION_START_H, 0)
int sessDow = dayofweek(sessStartNow, TZ)
int closeRef = sessDow == dayofweek.sunday ? sessStartNow - 2 * DAY_MS : sessDow == dayofweek.saturday ? sessStartNow - DAY_MS : sessStartNow
int prevClose = timestamp(TZ, year(closeRef, TZ), month(closeRef, TZ), dayofmonth(closeRef, TZ), SESSION_END_H, 0)
bool stale = iAsOf < prevClose
bool asOfFuture = iAsOf > timenow
bool curSess = time >= sessStartNow
// While the as-of time is in the future the whole current session is live (with a warning).
bool liveBar = curSess and (asOfFuture or time_close > iAsOf)
// "Draw only, no alerts" with stale or future figures mutes every alert, exits and reminders included.
bool muteAlerts = (stale or asOfFuture) and iStaleMode == STALE_QUIET

// --------------------------------------------- July NQ indicator stack -----
// Copied from the compiled July port (Apex 50K Eval Lab): same EMAs, Wilder
// ATR/RSI/ADX, session VWAP with volume-weighted bands, ATR percentile,
// pivots, 15m bias, prior-day levels, opening range, five setups and gates.
float emaF = ta.ema(close, 9)
float emaM = ta.ema(close, 21)
float emaS = ta.ema(close, 50)
float atrV = ta.atr(14)
float rsiV = ta.rsi(close, 14)
[diPlus, diMinus, adxV] = ta.dmi(14, 14)
[vwapV, vwapU1, vwapL1] = ta.vwap(hlc3, newDay, 1.0)
float vwapSd = vwapU1 - vwapV
float atrRank = ta.percentrank(atrV, 100)
float volAvgPrev = ta.sma(volume, 20)[1]
float rvol = na(volAvgPrev) or volAvgPrev <= 0 ? na : volume / volAvgPrev
float lo4 = ta.lowest(low, 4)
float hi4 = ta.highest(high, 4)
float lo10 = ta.lowest(low, 10)
float hi10 = ta.highest(high, 10)
float belowN = math.sum(close < vwapV ? 1 : 0, 6)[1]
float aboveN = math.sum(close > vwapV ? 1 : 0, 6)[1]

// 15-minute bias from the last completed 15m bar: close vs EMA21 with the
// EMA's 5-point least-squares slope agreeing (market.py _bias_from).
// lookahead_on with [1] gives the same completed bar historically and live.
htfBiasCalc() =>
    float e = ta.ema(close, 21)
    float slope = (2.0 * (e - e[4]) + (e[1] - e[3])) / 10.0
    int b = 0
    if not na(e)
        if close > e and (na(slope) or slope >= 0)
            b := 1
        else if close < e and (na(slope) or slope <= 0)
            b := -1
    b
int htfBiasRaw = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "15", htfBiasCalc()[1], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
int htfBias = nz(htfBiasRaw, 0)

// Prior trading day's high/low, computed on the chart (no request.security).
var float dayHi = na
var float dayLo = na
var float pdHigh = na
var float pdLow = na
if newDay
    if not na(dayHi)
        pdHigh := dayHi
        pdLow := dayLo
    dayHi := high
    dayLo := low
else
    dayHi := math.max(dayHi, high)
    dayLo := math.min(dayLo, low)

// Confirmed swing pivots (3 left / 3 right, ties allowed), published 3 bars late.
bool isPH = bar_index >= 6 and high <= high[3] and high[1] <= high[3] and high[2] <= high[3] and high[4] <= high[3] and high[5] <= high[3] and high[6] <= high[3]
bool isPL = bar_index >= 6 and low >= low[3] and low[1] >= low[3] and low[2] >= low[3] and low[4] >= low[3] and low[5] >= low[3] and low[6] >= low[3]
var float lastPH = na
var float lastPL = na
if isPH
    lastPH := high[3]
if isPL
    lastPL := low[3]

// Opening range 09:30-10:00 ET, complete once a bar opens at or after 10:00.
var float orHi = na
var float orLo = na
var bool orDone = false
if newDay
    orHi := na
    orLo := na
    orDone := false
if etMin >= 570 and etMin < 600
    orHi := na(orHi) ? high : math.max(orHi, high)
    orLo := na(orLo) ? low : math.min(orLo, low)
else if etMin >= 600 and not na(orHi)
    orDone := true

int emaStack = na(emaF) or na(emaM) or na(emaS) ? 0 : emaF > emaM and emaM > emaS ? 1 : emaF < emaM and emaM < emaS ? -1 : 0
int regime = not na(atrRank) and atrRank >= 90 ? REG_EXP : not na(atrRank) and atrRank <= 15 ? REG_QUIET : na(adxV) or na(diPlus) or na(diMinus) ? REG_CHOP : adxV >= 23 and diPlus > diMinus and emaStack >= 0 ? REG_UP : adxV >= 23 and diMinus > diPlus and emaStack <= 0 ? REG_DOWN : REG_CHOP
bool isRange = regime == REG_CHOP or regime == REG_QUIET
float closePos = high - low <= 0 ? 0.5 : (close - low) / (high - low)
bool warm = bar_index >= WARMUP_BARS and not na(emaS) and not na(atrV) and not na(adxV) and not na(vwapV) and not na(atrRank)

// Context support for a direction (signals.py _confluence).
confluence(int dir) =>
    float pts = 0.0
    pts += htfBias == dir ? 15 : htfBias == -dir ? -12 : 0
    pts += emaStack == dir ? 10 : emaStack == -dir ? -8 : 0
    if not na(vwapV)
        pts += (dir > 0 ? close > vwapV : close < vwapV) ? 10 : -6
    if not na(adxV)
        pts += math.max(0.0, math.min(15.0, (adxV - 15.0) * 0.9))
    if not na(rvol)
        pts += rvol >= 1.3 ? 10 : rvol < 0.7 ? -8 : 0
    pts += sessDrive or sessMorning ? 10 : sessLunch ? -15 : sessPower ? 5 : 0
    if not na(rsiV)
        pts += dir > 0 and rsiV > 78 ? -10 : dir < 0 and rsiV < 22 ? -10 : 0
    pts
float scoreL = confluence(1)
float scoreS = confluence(-1)

// Snap to ticks (stops and targets rounded the conservative way) and reject
// broken geometry (signals.py _build_setup).
buildSetup(int dir, float entryRaw, float stopRaw, float t1Raw, float t2Raw, float scoreRaw) =>
    float e = rNear(entryRaw)
    float s = dir > 0 ? rDown(stopRaw) : rUp(stopRaw)
    float a = dir > 0 ? rDown(t1Raw) : rUp(t1Raw)
    float b = dir > 0 ? rDown(t2Raw) : rUp(t2Raw)
    bool okNum = dir != 0 and not na(e) and not na(s) and not na(a) and not na(b) and not na(scoreRaw)
    bool okGeo = okNum and (dir > 0 ? s < e and e < a and a <= b : s > e and e > a and a >= b) and math.abs(e - s) >= syminfo.mintick
    [okGeo, e, s, a, b, math.max(0.0, math.min(100.0, nz(scoreRaw)))]

float stopStructL = (na(lastPL) ? lo10 : math.min(lastPL, lo10)) - 0.25 * atrV
float stopStructS = (na(lastPH) ? hi10 : math.max(lastPH, hi10)) + 0.25 * atrV

// 1. Trend Pullback (detect_trend_pullback)
int tpDir0 = regime == REG_UP ? 1 : regime == REG_DOWN ? -1 : 0
float refHi = na(vwapV) ? emaM : math.max(emaM, vwapV)
float refLo = na(vwapV) ? emaM : math.min(emaM, vwapV)
bool tpLong = tpDir0 == 1 and lo4 <= refHi + 0.35 * atrV and close > open and closePos >= 0.6 and close > emaM
bool tpShort = tpDir0 == -1 and hi4 >= refLo - 0.35 * atrV and close <= open and closePos <= 0.4 and close < emaM
int tpDir = not na(emaM) and (tpLong or tpShort) ? tpDir0 : 0
float tpStop = tpDir > 0 ? stopStructL : stopStructS
float tpRisk = math.abs(close - tpStop)
[tpOk, tpE, tpS, tpA, tpB, tpSc] = buildSetup(tpDir, close, tpStop, close + tpRisk * 1.5 * tpDir, close + tpRisk * 3.0 * tpDir, (tpDir > 0 ? scoreL : scoreS) + 22)

// 2. Opening Range Breakout (detect_orb_breakout)
float orW = orHi - orLo
bool orbGate = orDone and not na(orHi) and not na(orLo) and minsSinceOpen >= 30 and minsSinceOpen <= 180 and orW <= 3.0 * atrV and orW >= 0.4 * atrV and not isRange
int orbRaw = close > orHi and close[1] <= orHi ? 1 : close < orLo and close[1] >= orLo ? -1 : 0
bool orbBar = orbRaw == 1 ? closePos >= 0.55 : orbRaw == -1 ? closePos <= 0.45 : false
int orbDir = orbGate and orbBar ? orbRaw : 0
float orbStop = orbDir > 0 ? math.min(stopStructL, orHi - 0.3 * atrV) : math.max(stopStructS, orLo + 0.3 * atrV)
float orbRisk = math.abs(close - orbStop)
[orbOk, orbE, orbS, orbA, orbB, orbSc] = buildSetup(orbDir, close, orbStop, close + orbRisk * 1.5 * orbDir, close + math.max(orbRisk * 2.5, orW) * orbDir, (orbDir > 0 ? scoreL : scoreS) + 25)

// 3. VWAP Reclaim (detect_vwap_reclaim)
bool vrGate = bar_index >= 6 and not na(vwapV) and not na(vwapV[6]) and regime != REG_EXP
int vrRaw = belowN >= 4 and close > vwapV and close > open ? 1 : aboveN >= 4 and close < vwapV and close <= open ? -1 : 0
int vrDir = vrGate ? vrRaw : 0
float vrStop = vrDir > 0 ? math.min(stopStructL, vwapV - 0.4 * atrV) : math.max(stopStructS, vwapV + 0.4 * atrV)
float vrRisk = math.abs(close - vrStop)
[vrOk, vrE, vrS, vrA, vrB, vrSc] = buildSetup(vrDir, close, vrStop, close + vrRisk * 1.5 * vrDir, close + vrRisk * 2.5 * vrDir, (vrDir > 0 ? scoreL : scoreS) + 15)

// 4. Failed Breakout Reversal (detect_failed_breakout)
int fbRaw = not na(pdHigh) and hi4 > pdHigh and close < pdHigh ? -1 : not na(pdLow) and lo4 < pdLow and close > pdLow ? 1 : 0
float fbLevel = fbRaw < 0 ? hi4 : lo4
float fbRef = fbRaw < 0 ? pdHigh : pdLow
bool fbValid = bar_index >= 3 and fbRaw != 0 and math.abs(fbLevel - fbRef) >= 0.15 * atrV and (fbRaw > 0 ? close > open : close <= open)
int fbDir = fbValid ? fbRaw : 0
float fbStop = fbDir < 0 ? fbLevel + 0.3 * atrV : fbLevel - 0.3 * atrV
float fbRisk = math.abs(close - fbStop)
float fbT2 = not na(vwapV) and (vwapV - close) * fbDir > fbRisk * 2 ? vwapV : close + fbRisk * 2.5 * fbDir
[fbOk, fbE, fbS, fbA, fbB, fbSc] = buildSetup(fbDir, close, fbStop, close + fbRisk * 1.5 * fbDir, fbT2, (fbDir > 0 ? scoreL : scoreS) + 18)

// 5. VWAP Fade (detect_vwap_fade), range regimes only
float sigma = not na(vwapSd) and vwapSd > 0 ? (close - vwapV) / vwapSd : na
int fadeRaw = isRange and not na(sigma) and math.abs(sigma) >= 2.0 ? (sigma > 0 ? -1 : 1) : 0
float bodyAbs = math.abs(close - open)
bool fadeShortOk = (high - math.max(open, close) > bodyAbs * 0.8 or close <= open) and (na(rsiV) or rsiV > 62)
bool fadeLongOk = (math.min(open, close) - low > bodyAbs * 0.8 or close > open) and (na(rsiV) or rsiV < 38)
int fadeDir = fadeRaw < 0 and fadeShortOk ? -1 : fadeRaw > 0 and fadeLongOk ? 1 : 0
float fadeStop = fadeDir < 0 ? high + 0.5 * atrV : low - 0.5 * atrV
float fadeRisk = math.abs(close - fadeStop)
float fadeT1 = close + math.min(math.abs(close - vwapV) * 0.6, fadeRisk * 1.5) * fadeDir
[fadeOk, fadeE, fadeS, fadeA, fadeB, fadeSc] = buildSetup(fadeRisk > 0 ? fadeDir : 0, close, fadeStop, fadeT1, vwapV, (fadeDir > 0 ? scoreL : scoreS) + 12)

// Best enabled candidate by score; ties keep detector order (detect_all).
int jDir = 0
float jE = na
float jS = na
float jA = na
float jB = na
float jSc = -1.0
string jName = ""
if iUseTP and tpOk and tpSc > jSc
    jDir := tpDir
    jE := tpE
    jS := tpS
    jA := tpA
    jB := tpB
    jSc := tpSc
    jName := "Trend Pullback"
if iUseORB and orbOk and orbSc > jSc
    jDir := orbDir
    jE := orbE
    jS := orbS
    jA := orbA
    jB := orbB
    jSc := orbSc
    jName := "Opening Range Breakout"
if iUseVR and vrOk and vrSc > jSc
    jDir := vrDir
    jE := vrE
    jS := vrS
    jA := vrA
    jB := vrB
    jSc := vrSc
    jName := "VWAP Reclaim"
if iUseFB and fbOk and fbSc > jSc
    jDir := fbDir
    jE := fbE
    jS := fbS
    jA := fbA
    jB := fbB
    jSc := fbSc
    jName := "Failed Breakout Reversal"
if iUseFade and fadeOk and fadeSc > jSc
    jDir := fadeDir
    jE := fadeE
    jS := fadeS
    jA := fadeA
    jB := fadeB
    jSc := fadeSc
    jName := "VWAP Fade"
// July playbook gates on the best candidate only: score, stop sanity, net R.
float jStopPts = math.abs(jE - jS)
float jNetR = (math.abs(jA - jE) * pv - rtCost) / (jStopPts * pv + rtCost)
bool julyPass = jDir != 0 and jSc >= iMinScore and jStopPts >= iMinStop and jStopPts <= iMaxStop and jNetR >= iMinNetR

// =================================================== ACCOUNT GATES =========
// Day P&L = typed realized P&L (live bars only) + virtual P&L counted today
// (since the as-of time on live bars, since the session start on review
// bars) + the open virtual trade's P&L.
acctNow(bool live, float dVirt, float openPnl) =>
    // Stale figures come from an earlier session: their realized P&L is part of the balance, not of today.
    float typedToday = live and not stale ? iTodayPnl : 0.0
    float dayPnl = typedToday + dVirt + openPnl
    float room = iBal + (live ? iTodayPnl : 0.0) + dVirt + openPnl - floorUsed
    float dllRoom = na(planDll) ? float(na) : planDll + dayPnl
    bool dllHit = not na(planDll) and dayPnl <= -planDll
    bool selfHit = iSelfStop > 0 and dayPnl <= -iSelfStop
    bool lockHit = not na(lockVal) and dayPnl >= lockVal
    [dayPnl, room, dllRoom, dllHit, selfHit, lockHit]

// First reason that blocks a new prompt, or "" when armed.
gateWhy(bool live, bool warmOk, float room, bool dllHit, bool selfHit, bool lockHit, int trades, int streak, bool busy, bool inWin, bool nearFb) =>
    string r = ""
    if not warmOk
        r := "warming up"
    else if live and asOfFuture
        r := "as-of time is in the future"
    else if live and stale
        r := "STALE inputs (as-of before the previous session's 17:00 ET close)"
    else if room <= 0
        r := "at or below the drawdown floor"
    else if dllHit
        r := "daily loss limit hit"
    else if selfHit
        r := "daily stop hit"
    else if lockHit
        r := "daily profit lock reached"
    else if trades >= iMaxTrades
        r := str.tostring(trades) + " trades today (max " + str.tostring(iMaxTrades) + ")"
    else if streak >= iMaxLosses
        r := str.tostring(streak) + " losses in a row"
    else if busy
        r := "virtual trade open"
    else if not inWin
        r := "outside the entry window"
    else if nearFb
        r := "within 20 min of flat-by"
    r

// Size: the smallest budget over the per-contract risk, capped by the plan.
sizeFor(float stopPts, float room, float dllRoom, float dayPnl) =>
    float perC = (stopPts + 2 * slipPx) * pv + rtCost
    float budget = iRisk
    string bind = "risk per trade"
    float bFloor = room * iShare / 100.0
    if bFloor < budget
        budget := bFloor
        bind := str.tostring(iShare) + "% of floor room"
    if not na(dllRoom) and dllRoom - DLL_MARGIN < budget
        budget := dllRoom - DLL_MARGIN
        bind := "DLL room - $100"
    if iSelfStop > 0 and iSelfStop + dayPnl < budget
        budget := iSelfStop + dayPnl
        bind := "daily stop room"
    int q = na(perC) or perC <= 0 ? 0 : int(math.floor(budget / perC))
    q := math.max(0, math.min(capQty, q))
    [q, perC, budget, bind]

// ======================================================== VIRTUAL TRADE ======
type VTrade
    int dir = 0
    float qty0 = 0.0
    float qty = 0.0
    float entry = na
    float stop = na
    float t1 = na
    float t2 = na
    bool scaled = false
    int bars = 0
    float net = 0.0
    string name = ""
    float score = 0.0
    bool live = false
    int bar0 = 0
    float barPnl = 0.0
    string barTxt = ""
    string barTag = ""
    float barPx = na
    bool closedNow = false

method resetBar(VTrade v) =>
    v.barPnl := 0.0
    v.barTxt := ""
    v.barTag := ""
    v.barPx := na
    v.closedNow := false

method start(VTrade v, int dir, float qty, float fillPx, float stopPx, float t1Px, float t2Px, string name, float score, bool live) =>
    v.dir := dir
    v.qty0 := qty
    v.qty := qty
    v.entry := fillPx
    v.stop := stopPx
    v.t1 := t1Px
    v.t2 := t2Px
    v.scaled := false
    v.bars := 0
    v.net := 0.0
    v.name := name
    v.score := score
    v.live := live
    v.bar0 := bar_index

// Close qtyLeg contracts at px and book the leg, net of round-trip commission.
method leg(VTrade v, string tag, float qtyLeg, float px) =>
    float pnl = qtyLeg * v.dir * (px - v.entry) * pv - qtyLeg * rtCost
    v.net += pnl
    v.qty -= qtyLeg
    v.barPnl += pnl
    v.barTxt := v.barTxt + (v.barTxt == "" ? "" : ", ") + tag + " " + str.tostring(qtyLeg, "#") + " @ " + str.tostring(px, format.mintick)
    v.barTag := v.barTag + (v.barTag == "" ? "" : "+") + tag
    v.barPx := px
    if v.qty <= 0
        v.closedNow := true
    pnl

// One bar of management, in the order of the July backtest (_manage).
method manage(VTrade v, bool flatNow) =>
    v.bars += 1
    float d = v.dir
    bool gapped = d > 0 ? open <= v.stop : open >= v.stop
    bool stopHit = d > 0 ? low <= v.stop : high >= v.stop
    bool t1Hit = d > 0 ? high >= v.t1 : low <= v.t1
    bool t2Hit = d > 0 ? high >= v.t2 : low <= v.t2
    if gapped
        v.leg("GAP STOP", v.qty, open)
    else if stopHit
        v.leg(v.scaled ? "BE STOP" : "STOP", v.qty, v.stop - d * slipPx)
    else
        if t1Hit and not v.scaled and v.qty >= 2
            v.leg("T1", math.floor(v.qty / 2), v.t1)
            v.scaled := true
            v.stop := v.entry
        if t2Hit
            v.leg("T2", v.qty, v.t2)
        else if t1Hit and not v.scaled
            v.leg("T1", v.qty, v.t1)
        else if flatNow
            v.leg("FLAT-BY", v.qty, close - d * slipPx)
        else if v.bars >= TIME_STOP_BARS
            v.leg("TIME", v.qty, close - d * slipPx)
    v.closedNow

method openPnl(VTrade v) =>
    v.dir != 0 ? v.qty * v.dir * (close - v.entry) * pv : 0.0

exitText(VTrade v, float dayPnl) =>
    string side = v.dir > 0 ? "LONG" : "SHORT"
    string tail = v.closedNow ? " | trade " + fmtSigned(v.net) : " | trade so far " + fmtSigned(v.net) + " | runner " + str.tostring(v.qty, "#") + " " + side + ", stop moved to breakeven " + fmtPx(v.stop)
    syminfo.root + " EXIT " + v.barTxt + " (" + side + " " + v.name + ") | virtual P&L " + fmtSigned(v.barPnl) + tail + " | day " + fmtSigned(dayPnl) + " | " + tagTxt

// Keep at most MAX_KEEP_LABELS labels, deleting the oldest.
keepLabel(array<label> a, label l) =>
    a.push(l)
    if a.size() > MAX_KEEP_LABELS
        label.delete(a.shift())
    l

exitMark(VTrade v, array<label> a) =>
    color c = v.barPnl > 0 ? color.teal : v.barPnl < 0 ? color.red : color.gray
    keepLabel(a, label.new(bar_index, v.barPx, v.barTag + " " + fmtSigned(v.barPnl), style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(c, v.live ? 10 : 55), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny))

moveLine(line l, int x1, int x2, float y, color c) =>
    line.set_xy1(l, x1, y)
    line.set_xy2(l, x2, y)
    line.set_color(l, c)

showMark(bool live) =>
    live or iShowReview

// ================================================================ STATE ======
var VTrade vt = VTrade.new()
var int pDir = 0
var float pQty = 0.0
var float pEst = na
var float pStop = na
var float pT1 = na
var float pT2 = na
var string pName = ""
var float pScore = 0.0
var bool pLive = false
var int pBar = 0

var float dayVirt = 0.0
var int dayTrades = 0
var int lossStreak = 0
var bool liveStarted = false
var bool fbWarned = false
var int nPosted = 0
var int nPaused = 0
var int nNoSize = 0
var string lastPauseWhy = ""
var string lastSigTxt = "-"
var array<label> labs = array.new<label>()

var line lnE = line.new(bar_index, close, bar_index + 1, close, color = color.new(color.gray, 100), width = 2)
var line lnS = line.new(bar_index, close, bar_index + 1, close, color = color.new(color.gray, 100), width = 2)
var line lnA = line.new(bar_index, close, bar_index + 1, close, color = color.new(color.gray, 100), width = 1, style = line.style_dashed)
var line lnB = line.new(bar_index, close, bar_index + 1, close, color = color.new(color.gray, 100), width = 1, style = line.style_dashed)

bool longNow = false
bool shortNow = false
bool blockedNow = false
int blockedDir = 0
int noSizeDir = 0
bool longAlert = false
bool shortAlert = false
bool exitAlert = false
bool fbWarnNow = false
float exitMarkPx = na
string alertTxt = ""

// ============================================================= EACH BAR ======
// Everything below runs on confirmed bars only, so within a session the
// history and the live chart follow the same path. Which bars are live
// depends on timenow and the typed figures: after the session rolls, a
// reload or new inputs, earlier bars are recomputed as review bars and can
// differ from what was alerted.
if barstate.isconfirmed
    vt.resetBar()

    // A. New session: a virtual trade still open is closed at this open, and
    //    the day counters reset.
    if newDay
        if vt.dir != 0
            vt.leg("SESSION END", vt.qty, open)
            float dpEnd = (vt.live and not stale ? iTodayPnl : 0.0) + dayVirt + vt.barPnl
            if showMark(vt.live)
                exitMark(vt, labs)
                exitMarkPx := vt.barPx
            if vt.live and not muteAlerts
                alertTxt := addLine(alertTxt, exitText(vt, dpEnd))
                exitAlert := true
            vt.dir := 0
        vt.resetBar()
        pDir := 0
        dayVirt := 0.0
        dayTrades := 0
        lossStreak := 0
        liveStarted := false
        fbWarned := false
        nPosted := 0
        nPaused := 0
        nNoSize := 0
        lastPauseWhy := ""

    // B. The first bar that closes after the as-of time switches the day's
    //    counters to the typed figures (virtual P&L counts from here on). A
    //    review trade or prompt still open or pending is dropped: no alert
    //    was sent for it, and the typed figures already hold what happened.
    if liveBar and not liveStarted
        liveStarted := true
        if vt.dir != 0 and not vt.live
            vt.dir := 0
        if pDir != 0 and not pLive
            pDir := 0
        dayVirt := 0.0
        dayTrades := stale ? 0 : iTradesToday
        lossStreak := 0

    // C. A pending prompt fills at this bar's open + 1 tick, unless that is
    //    already past its stop or its target 1.
    if pDir != 0
        float fillPx = rNear(open + pDir * slipPx)
        bool pastStop = pDir > 0 ? fillPx <= pStop : fillPx >= pStop
        bool pastT1 = pDir > 0 ? fillPx >= pT1 : fillPx <= pT1
        if not pastStop and not pastT1
            vt.start(pDir, pQty, fillPx, pStop, pT1, pT2, pName, pScore, pLive)
            dayTrades += 1
        else
            string pastWhat = pastStop ? "the stop" : "target 1"
            if showMark(pLive)
                keepLabel(labs, label.new(bar_index, open, "cancelled: opened past " + pastWhat, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(color.gray, 30), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny))
            if pLive and liveBar and not muteAlerts
                alertTxt := addLine(alertTxt, syminfo.root + " CANCEL " + (pDir > 0 ? "LONG" : "SHORT") + " " + pName + ": the bar opened at " + fmtPx(open) + ", past " + pastWhat + " " + fmtPx(pastStop ? pStop : pT1) + " - do not enter | " + tagTxt)
                exitAlert := true
        pDir := 0

    // D. Manage the virtual trade on this bar, its fill bar included.
    if vt.dir != 0
        vt.manage(atFlatBy)
        if vt.barTxt != ""
            dayVirt += vt.barPnl
            if vt.closedNow
                lossStreak := vt.net < 0 ? lossStreak + 1 : 0
            float dpNow = (liveBar and not stale ? iTodayPnl : 0.0) + dayVirt
            if showMark(vt.live)
                exitMark(vt, labs)
                exitMarkPx := vt.barPx
            if vt.live and liveBar and not muteAlerts
                alertTxt := addLine(alertTxt, exitText(vt, dpNow))
                exitAlert := true
            if vt.closedNow
                vt.dir := 0

    // E. Flat-by reminder, once per session, about 10 minutes before.
    if fbWarnBar and not fbWarned
        fbWarned := true
        if liveBar and not muteAlerts
            fbWarnNow := true
            string openTxt = vt.dir != 0 ? " | virtual " + (vt.dir > 0 ? "LONG " : "SHORT ") + str.tostring(vt.qty, "#") + " still open, trade P&L " + fmtSigned(vt.net + vt.openPnl()) : ""
            string staleTxt = asOfFuture ? " | as-of time is in the future: fix it so sizes use today's figures" : stale ? " | account figures STALE: sizes use old figures until you type today's figures and as-of time and recreate the alert" : ""
            alertTxt := addLine(alertTxt, syminfo.root + " FLAT-BY in 10 min: be flat by " + flatTxt + " ET" + openTxt + staleTxt + " | " + tagTxt)

    // F. A new prompt from the best July setup that passed its gates. Every setup that passes the setup rules
    // is drawn: stale or future account figures only add a warning (and, per the input, mute the alert); an
    // account limit draws it in grey with the reason; window, warm-up, flat-by and an open virtual trade hide it.
    if julyPass
        [dP, rF, rD, hD, hS, hL] = acctNow(liveBar, dayVirt, vt.openPnl())
        bool figWarn = liveBar and (stale or asOfFuture)
        // live = false skips the stale / future checks inside gateWhy: they are handled as a warning here
        string why = gateWhy(false, warm, rF, hD, hS, hL, dayTrades, lossStreak, vt.dir != 0 or pDir != 0, inWindow, nearFlatBy)
        // not drawn at all: warm-up, a signal still pending or open, outside the entry window, near the flat-by
        bool quietWhy = not warm or vt.dir != 0 or pDir != 0 or not inWindow or nearFlatBy
        string side = jDir > 0 ? "LONG" : "SHORT"
        string scoreTxt = jName + " " + str.tostring(jSc, "#")
        string warnTxt = figWarn ? (asOfFuture ? "as-of time in the future" : "ACCOUNT FIGURES STALE") : ""
        bool alertOk = liveBar and not muteAlerts
        if why != ""
            if curSess
                nPaused += 1
                lastPauseWhy := scoreTxt + ": " + why
            if iShowBlocked and not quietWhy and showMark(liveBar)
                blockedNow := true
                blockedDir := jDir
                string bTxt = side + " setup held back\n" + why + "\n" + scoreTxt + (liveBar ? "" : "  (past)")
                keepLabel(labs, label.new(bar_index, jDir > 0 ? low : high, bTxt, yloc = jDir > 0 ? yloc.belowbar : yloc.abovebar, style = jDir > 0 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = color.new(color.gray, 25), textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny))
        else
            [q, perC, budget, bind] = sizeFor(jStopPts, rF, rD, dP)
            if q < 1
                if curSess
                    nNoSize += 1
                    lastPauseWhy := scoreTxt + ": no size (" + bind + ")"
                if showMark(liveBar)
                    noSizeDir := jDir
                    string hint = isMicro ? "lower the stop or raise risk per trade" : "chart the micro (MNQ) or raise risk per trade"
                    string nsTxt = side + " @ " + fmtPx(jE) + "  SL " + fmtPx(jS) + "\nno size: " + bind + " " + fmtUsd0(budget) + " < " + fmtUsd2(perC) + "/contract (" + hint + ")\n" + scoreTxt + (liveBar ? (figWarn ? "\n" + warnTxt : "") : "  (past)")
                    keepLabel(labs, label.new(bar_index, jDir > 0 ? low : high, nsTxt, yloc = jDir > 0 ? yloc.belowbar : yloc.abovebar, style = jDir > 0 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = color.new(jDir > 0 ? color.teal : color.red, 45), textcolor = color.white, size = lblSize))
            else
                pDir := jDir
                pQty := q
                pEst := jE
                pStop := jS
                pT1 := jA
                pT2 := jB
                pName := jName
                pScore := jSc
                pLive := liveBar
                pBar := bar_index
                if curSess
                    nPosted += 1
                lastSigTxt := str.format_time(time_close, "MM-dd HH:mm", TZ) + " " + side + " " + str.tostring(q) + " @ " + fmtPx(jE) + " " + scoreTxt + (liveBar ? (figWarn ? " (" + warnTxt + ")" : "") : " (past)")
                if showMark(liveBar)
                    longNow := jDir > 0
                    shortNow := jDir < 0
                    color base = jDir > 0 ? color.teal : color.red
                    string lt = side + " " + str.tostring(q) + " @ " + fmtPx(jE) + "\nSL " + fmtPx(jS) + "  T1 " + fmtPx(jA) + "  T2 " + fmtPx(jB) + "\n" + scoreTxt + (liveBar ? (figWarn ? "\n" + warnTxt + ": check size" : "") : "  (past)")
                    keepLabel(labs, label.new(bar_index, jDir > 0 ? low : high, lt, yloc = jDir > 0 ? yloc.belowbar : yloc.abovebar, style = jDir > 0 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = color.new(figWarn ? color.orange : base, 0), textcolor = color.white, size = lblSize))
                if alertOk
                    longAlert := jDir > 0
                    shortAlert := jDir < 0
                    string msg = (figWarn ? warnTxt + ": size uses old figures, check your Tradeify floor and DLL room first | " : "") + syminfo.root + " " + side + " " + str.tostring(q) + " @ " + fmtPx(jE) + " | stop " + fmtPx(jS) + " (" + str.tostring(jStopPts, "#,##0.00") + " pts, " + fmtUsd2(q * perC) + " risk) | T1 " + fmtPx(jA) + " | T2 " + fmtPx(jB) + " | " + scoreTxt + " | floor room " + fmtUsd0(rF) + " | DLL room " + fmtUsd0(rD) + " | " + tagTxt
                    alertTxt := addLine(alertTxt, msg)

    // G. Entry, stop, T1 and T2 lines while a prompt is pending or open.
    bool lnOn = vt.dir != 0 or pDir != 0
    bool lnLive = vt.dir != 0 ? vt.live : pLive
    if lnOn and showMark(lnLive)
        int x1 = vt.dir != 0 ? vt.bar0 : pBar
        int x2 = bar_index + 5
        int tr = lnLive ? 0 : 50
        moveLine(lnE, x1, x2, vt.dir != 0 ? vt.entry : pEst, color.new(color.blue, tr))
        moveLine(lnS, x1, x2, vt.dir != 0 ? vt.stop : pStop, color.new(color.red, tr))
        moveLine(lnA, x1, x2, vt.dir != 0 ? vt.t1 : pT1, color.new(color.teal, vt.dir != 0 and vt.scaled ? 80 : tr))
        moveLine(lnB, x1, x2, vt.dir != 0 ? vt.t2 : pT2, color.new(color.teal, tr))
    else
        line.set_color(lnE, color.new(color.gray, 100))
        line.set_color(lnS, color.new(color.gray, 100))
        line.set_color(lnA, color.new(color.gray, 100))
        line.set_color(lnB, color.new(color.gray, 100))

    // H. One alert() per bar close with every message of the bar.
    if alertTxt != ""
        alert(alertTxt, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// ============================================================== MARKERS ======
plotshape(longNow, "Long signal", shape.triangleup, location.belowbar, color.teal, size = size.small, text = "LONG", textcolor = color.teal)
plotshape(shortNow, "Short signal", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color.red, size = size.small, text = "SHORT", textcolor = color.red)
plotshape(noSizeDir > 0, "Long setup, no size", shape.triangleup, location.belowbar, color.new(color.teal, 60), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(noSizeDir < 0, "Short setup, no size", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color.new(color.red, 60), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(blockedNow and blockedDir > 0, "Long setup held back", shape.triangleup, location.belowbar, color.new(color.gray, 20), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(blockedNow and blockedDir < 0, "Short setup held back", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color.new(color.gray, 20), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(exitMarkPx, "Virtual exit", shape.xcross, location.absolute, color.new(color.gray, 0), size = size.tiny)

alertcondition(longAlert, "Long signal", "Tradeify 50K Signals: LONG prompt on {{ticker}} at {{close}}. Size, stop and targets are on the chart and in the alert() message.")
alertcondition(shortAlert, "Short signal", "Tradeify 50K Signals: SHORT prompt on {{ticker}} at {{close}}. Size, stop and targets are on the chart and in the alert() message.")
alertcondition(exitAlert, "Exit", "Tradeify 50K Signals: virtual exit or cancel on {{ticker}} at {{close}}. See the chart for which exit and the P&L.")
alertcondition(fbWarnNow, "Flat-by in 10 minutes", "Tradeify 50K Signals: flat-by in 10 minutes on {{ticker}} ({{close}}). Be flat by the flat-by time.")

// ================================================================ TABLE ======
var table tb = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 14, bgcolor = color.new(color.black, 15), frame_color = color.new(color.gray, 50), frame_width = 1, border_color = color.new(color.gray, 75), border_width = 1)

tcell(int r, string k, string v, color vc) =>
    table.cell(tb, 0, r, k, text_color = color.new(color.silver, 0), text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(tb, 1, r, v, text_color = vc, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)

if barstate.islast and iShowTable
    float tOpen = vt.openPnl()
    [tDay, tRoom, tDllRoom, tDllHit, tSelf, tLock] = acctNow(liveBar, dayVirt, tOpen)
    string tFig = asOfFuture ? "as-of time in the future" : stale ? "STALE figures: sizes use old figures; type today's dashboard figures and as-of time" : ""
    string tWhy = not curSess ? "waiting for the session (18:00 ET)" : not liveBar ? "no bar has closed after the as-of time yet" : gateWhy(false, warm, tRoom, tDllHit, tSelf, tLock, dayTrades, lossStreak, vt.dir != 0 or pDir != 0, inWindow, nearFlatBy)
    // A budget that cannot size 1 contract even at the minimum stop posts nothing.
    if tWhy == ""
        [mq, mPerC, mBudget, mBind] = sizeFor(iMinStop, tRoom, tDllRoom, tDay)
        if mq < 1
            tWhy := mBind + " " + fmtUsd2(mBudget) + " cannot size 1 " + syminfo.root + " even at a " + str.tostring(iMinStop) + "-pt stop (needs " + fmtUsd2(mPerC) + ")" + (mBind == "risk per trade" and not isMicro ? ": use the micro contract or raise the risk" : "")
    string status = (tWhy == "" ? (muteAlerts ? "DRAW ONLY (alerts muted)" : "ARMED") : "PAUSED: " + tWhy) + (tFig != "" ? " | " + tFig : "")
    color white = color.new(color.white, 0)
    color good = color.new(color.lime, 0)
    color warnC = color.new(color.orange, 0)
    color bad = color.new(color.red, 0)
    table.cell(tb, 0, 0, tagTxt + " | " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, text_color = color.new(color.orange, 0), text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(tb, 0, 0, 1, 0)
    tcell(1, "Figures as of", str.format_time(iAsOf, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm", TZ) + " ET" + (stale ? "  STALE" : asOfFuture ? "  (future)" : ""), stale or asOfFuture ? bad : white)
    tcell(2, "Plan", planName + (isSelect ? ", tier from EOD profit " + fmtUsd0(eodProfit) : ""), white)
    tcell(3, "Floor", fmtUsd0(floorUsed) + (floorUsed >= TMD_LOCKED_FLOOR ? " (locked)" : "") + (floorTypedLow ? "  typed " + fmtUsd0(iFloor) + " is below the rule: check it" : ""), floorTypedLow ? warnC : white)
    tcell(4, "Room to floor", fmtUsd0(tRoom) + (liveBar ? "" : " (not live)"), tRoom <= 0 ? bad : tRoom < 500 ? warnC : white)
    tcell(5, "DLL room", na(planDll) ? "no DLL on this plan" : fmtUsd0(tDllRoom) + " of " + fmtUsd0(planDll) + (tDllHit ? "  HIT" : ""), tDllHit ? bad : white)
    tcell(6, "Size cap", str.tostring(capQty) + " " + syminfo.root + (isMicro ? " (" + str.tostring(capMinis) + " minis)" : ""), white)
    tcell(7, "Today's P&L", liveBar ? fmtSigned(tDay) + " (typed " + fmtSigned(iTodayPnl) + " + virtual " + fmtSigned(dayVirt + tOpen) + ")" : "virtual " + fmtSigned(tDay) + " (not live)", tDay < 0 ? warnC : white)
    tcell(8, "Day limits", "risk " + fmtUsd0(iRisk) + " / " + str.tostring(iShare) + "% of room | stop " + (iSelfStop > 0 ? fmtUsd0(iSelfStop) : "off") + " | lock " + (na(lockVal) ? "off" : fmtUsd0(lockVal)), white)
    tcell(9, "Trades today", str.tostring(dayTrades) + " / " + str.tostring(iMaxTrades) + " | losses in a row " + str.tostring(lossStreak) + " / " + str.tostring(iMaxLosses), white)
    tcell(10, "Status", status, tWhy == "" and tFig == "" ? good : warnC)
    tcell(11, "Setups this session", "posted " + str.tostring(nPosted) + ", paused " + str.tostring(nPaused) + ", no size " + str.tostring(nNoSize) + (lastPauseWhy != "" ? "\nlast held: " + lastPauseWhy : ""), white)
    tcell(12, "Last signal", lastSigTxt, white)
    table.cell(tb, 0, 13, "Unproven signals: prompts, not advice", text_color = color.new(color.silver, 0), text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.merge_cells(tb, 0, 13, 1, 13)
